WEBVTT

00:01:46.890 --> 00:01:48.760
What horrible defense.

00:01:50.450 --> 00:01:55.120
But now I can tell that you guys really want to play.

00:01:55.120 --> 00:01:56.230
You all pass!

00:01:56.740 --> 00:01:58.380
All right!

00:01:58.380 --> 00:01:59.900
Thank god!

00:02:00.380 --> 00:02:04.020
Starting tomorrow, we're going to start training for real.

00:02:04.020 --> 00:02:05.930
It's a team made up of beginners,

00:02:05.930 --> 00:02:09.610
but we're planning on making you competitive by spring.

00:02:10.250 --> 00:02:11.580
The first two months,

00:02:11.580 --> 00:02:15.060
we'll work on raising your stamina and strengthening your basics.

00:02:15.060 --> 00:02:18.330
Running properly, throwing properly, and hitting properly...

00:02:18.940 --> 00:02:22.090
We're going to force you to remember the essentials of baseball!

00:02:22.090 --> 00:02:25.910
We don't have time. Don't waste a single swing!

00:02:25.910 --> 00:02:26.500
Got it!?

00:02:26.500 --> 00:02:27.300
Yes!

00:02:29.110 --> 00:02:30.630
Yamada-sensei,

00:02:30.630 --> 00:02:33.470
for now, being strict seems to be going well,

00:02:34.250 --> 00:02:38.810
and Goro seems to have understood our message a little, hasn't he?

00:02:39.240 --> 00:02:44.970
Who knows? Right now, we can only encourage them.

00:02:44.970 --> 00:02:49.400
He has to figure out the real answer on his own from now on.

00:02:52.060 --> 00:02:56.840
So, until then, I'll work hard to build a foundation for him.

00:03:06.470 --> 00:03:09.010
They seem to be getting used to handling the ball,

00:03:09.010 --> 00:03:11.020
and have better stamina.

00:03:11.620 --> 00:03:12.500
All right.

00:03:12.500 --> 00:03:15.100
We're going to start training for games today.

00:03:22.010 --> 00:03:22.880
Amazing!

00:03:22.880 --> 00:03:24.960
Are we going to have to do that too?

00:03:24.960 --> 00:03:25.780
All right, next!

00:03:28.390 --> 00:03:29.790
Next is batting.

00:03:29.790 --> 00:03:31.200
Goro, get up on the mound.

00:03:31.580 --> 00:03:32.160
Got it!

00:03:32.590 --> 00:03:35.020
One by one, stand in the batter's box.

00:03:35.020 --> 00:03:38.390
Goro, pretend that it's a real game and throw in tough locations.

00:03:38.390 --> 00:03:40.470
I don't care if you pitch at full strength.

00:03:40.470 --> 00:03:42.750
This is your pitching practice as well.

00:03:42.750 --> 00:03:43.790
Okay.

00:03:43.790 --> 00:03:44.420
Are you serious?

00:03:49.610 --> 00:03:50.610
Um...

00:03:50.610 --> 00:03:54.180
I don't think these guys will be able to hit those kinds of pitches.

00:03:54.180 --> 00:03:55.970
They don't have to hit them.

00:03:57.710 --> 00:03:59.670
<i>Even if they can't hit it now,</i>

00:03:59.670 --> 00:04:01.600
<i>if they're watching these pitches every day,</i>

00:04:01.600 --> 00:04:03.860
<i>they'll get used to the speed of the ball.</i>

00:04:03.860 --> 00:04:06.440
<i>It's unconventional, but it's good practice. </i>

00:04:11.230 --> 00:04:12.950
Um, excuse me.

00:04:13.580 --> 00:04:16.660
Do you know where the baseball team practices?

00:04:19.290 --> 00:04:23.750
Hey! Don't do whatever you want just because my dad took a break today!

00:04:25.820 --> 00:04:26.960
I know!

00:04:30.540 --> 00:04:34.880
<i>Hey, hey, I thought they were joking, but they're seriously practicing on the roof?</i>

00:04:36.660 --> 00:04:39.460
How horrible! You suck.

00:04:43.390 --> 00:04:44.980
What'd you just say?

00:04:44.980 --> 00:04:47.260
Oh, did you hear me?

00:04:47.920 --> 00:04:50.700
Who are you? You're not one of our students, are you?

00:04:51.350 --> 00:04:52.820
Yeah, well...

00:04:52.820 --> 00:04:55.150
Is Shigeno-san here right now?

00:04:56.330 --> 00:04:57.450
Who are you?

00:04:58.550 --> 00:05:00.500
So you're Shigeno-san, huh?

00:05:00.500 --> 00:05:02.940
You do have the build.

00:05:02.940 --> 00:05:03.830
What'd you say?

00:05:03.830 --> 00:05:05.630
What's with this guy?

00:05:05.630 --> 00:05:08.040
He must be some spy from another baseball team.

00:05:09.250 --> 00:05:13.010
There's no point in spying on a baseball team that sucks.

00:05:13.800 --> 00:05:15.010
This kid!

00:05:15.990 --> 00:05:16.720
You bastard!

00:05:16.720 --> 00:05:18.210
Wait!

00:05:19.970 --> 00:05:24.250
You're talking as if you know me...

00:05:24.250 --> 00:05:25.440
What do you want?

00:05:27.940 --> 00:05:30.770
I came to test Shigeno Goro-san.

00:05:30.770 --> 00:05:32.480
What?

00:05:33.000 --> 00:05:34.660
Why don't we have a competition?

00:05:34.660 --> 00:05:36.670
If you can get three strikes against me,

00:05:36.670 --> 00:05:38.950
I'll tell you what I came here to do.

00:05:39.890 --> 00:05:41.410
A competition?

00:05:42.830 --> 00:05:45.870
Who are you starting a competition against, you spying prick?

00:05:45.870 --> 00:05:49.580
Are you saying this knowing that he went to Kaido?

00:05:49.580 --> 00:05:51.260
I know.

00:05:51.260 --> 00:05:55.800
But since you couldn't get the ace number, you ran away and came here, is that correct?

00:05:58.000 --> 00:05:59.190
So what'll you do?

00:06:02.160 --> 00:06:04.220
I'll end it in three pitches.

00:06:04.220 --> 00:06:06.520
If you aren't frightened out of your wits,

00:06:06.520 --> 00:06:09.400
come at me with all you've got, damn kid.

00:06:14.280 --> 00:06:15.360
All right, go ahead.

00:06:19.320 --> 00:06:21.740
If you can even graze it...

00:06:22.740 --> 00:06:24.120
try it!

00:06:26.080 --> 00:06:27.250
That's a strike, okay?

00:06:29.610 --> 00:06:31.230
<i>So fast! </i>

00:06:31.230 --> 00:06:33.340
<i>This is Shigeno Goro, huh?</i>

00:06:36.170 --> 00:06:37.630
Two strikes.

00:06:37.630 --> 00:06:39.700
Hey, hey, what's wrong?

00:06:39.700 --> 00:06:41.090
If you don't swing, you can't hit it!

00:06:42.300 --> 00:06:43.730
<i>I see.</i>

00:06:43.730 --> 00:06:46.270
<i>Well then, this might be worth betting on.</i>

00:06:46.990 --> 00:06:48.230
<i>It's over!</i>

00:06:50.350 --> 00:06:51.060
He hit it!

00:06:54.520 --> 00:06:56.480
Bah. Only to short, huh?

00:06:57.180 --> 00:06:58.210
<i>This kid...</i>

00:06:58.210 --> 00:06:59.610
<i>That wasn't luck.</i>

00:06:59.610 --> 00:07:01.450
<i>He was watching and hit it.</i>

00:07:02.670 --> 00:07:04.740
Well, you aren't that big of a deal... 

00:07:04.740 --> 00:07:07.370
since you can't get three strikes against a junior high student like me.

00:07:07.370 --> 00:07:08.330
What!?

00:07:08.330 --> 00:07:10.040
Junior high!?

00:07:10.040 --> 00:07:14.000
But... I guess I like it. There's not a whole lot of members,

00:07:14.440 --> 00:07:17.460
and it's not a traditional school with a lot of graduates or coaches telling me what to do.

00:07:18.010 --> 00:07:19.020
All right.

00:07:19.020 --> 00:07:22.680
I'll enroll at Seishuu and become part of the baseball team.

00:07:23.390 --> 00:07:24.600
What!?

00:07:24.600 --> 00:07:26.730
Well then, see you later.

00:07:27.480 --> 00:07:30.790
Oh. Keep the starting shortstop position open please.

00:07:30.790 --> 00:07:32.560
Hey! Wait a second!

00:07:32.560 --> 00:07:33.800
Who the heck are you?

00:07:33.800 --> 00:07:36.440
Who did you hear about me from?

00:07:39.290 --> 00:07:40.410
Shimizu!

00:07:40.410 --> 00:07:42.320
Yo! You were here already?

00:07:43.490 --> 00:07:47.430
So, how was it? Did you get to see our ace's pitching?

00:07:47.430 --> 00:07:53.460
Yeah, he doesn't seem like an idiot that's just trying to beat Kaido.

00:07:53.460 --> 00:07:56.810
Just like you said, sister, if I come here, it seems like I'll have fun.

00:07:56.810 --> 00:07:57.960
I see.

00:07:59.420 --> 00:08:01.880
S-Sister?

00:08:01.880 --> 00:08:04.840
No way! Kaoru-chan's his sister?

00:08:05.430 --> 00:08:08.560
This kid's my little brother, Shimizu Taiga.

00:08:09.150 --> 00:08:13.830
He's a little cocky but he was a regular for five years straight on the Yokohama Senior League team,

00:08:13.830 --> 00:08:15.760
so his skills are for real.

00:08:17.330 --> 00:08:19.690
Oh, <i>that</i> Shimizu?

00:08:20.070 --> 00:08:21.530
You know him, old man?

00:08:21.530 --> 00:08:23.000
Of course.

00:08:23.000 --> 00:08:25.900
I looked after him for three years in Little League after all.

00:08:26.430 --> 00:08:27.440
I see...

00:08:27.440 --> 00:08:34.040
I heard he'd taken a sports scholarship for Kaido, but he refused and is entering Seishuu, huh?

00:08:34.040 --> 00:08:35.130
Yup, that seems like him.

00:08:35.130 --> 00:08:37.010
Kaido's sports scholarship?

00:08:37.010 --> 00:08:38.380
What kind of player is he?

00:08:39.190 --> 00:08:41.880
He doesn't have power, but he's fast.

00:08:41.880 --> 00:08:45.150
He's the type that's extremely flexible and has good reflexes, so he makes a good lead-off batter.

00:08:45.150 --> 00:08:47.600
He shouldn't have a problem being the shortstop.

00:08:48.130 --> 00:08:51.810
I didn't know that Shimizu had a little brother like that.

00:08:51.810 --> 00:08:56.070
If that kind of guy becomes the ninth member of our team, I'd have no complaints!

00:08:56.070 --> 00:08:59.880
Then we'll need to hurry and determine everyone else's positions.

00:08:59.880 --> 00:09:01.100
That's right.

00:09:01.100 --> 00:09:02.440
Positions?

00:09:02.440 --> 00:09:07.030
Everyone other than Tashiro is a beginner. Shouldn't we watch their development carefully before deciding? 

00:09:07.400 --> 00:09:09.420
It's because they're beginners.

00:09:09.420 --> 00:09:12.520
We have to decide on their positions as soon as possible, so even if they're horrible at everything else...

00:09:12.520 --> 00:09:16.720
we can specially train them to be good at their specific positions.

00:09:16.720 --> 00:09:19.250
That's because there's no time for them to gain experience slowly.

00:09:20.290 --> 00:09:22.210
You decide, Goro.

00:09:22.210 --> 00:09:23.420
Me!?

00:09:24.000 --> 00:09:27.280
You're the one who has to be able to trust them.

00:09:27.280 --> 00:09:30.600
There's always a strength and a significant personality trait to a person.

00:09:30.600 --> 00:09:33.180
That's up to you to figure out.

00:09:35.590 --> 00:09:38.020
Strengths and personality traits, huh?

00:09:38.490 --> 00:09:43.110
Uchiyama said that he played basketball when he was in junior high, right?

00:09:43.110 --> 00:09:44.020
Yeah.

00:09:44.500 --> 00:09:47.870
<i>With experience in athletics, his agility is good.</i>

00:09:47.870 --> 00:09:50.740
<i>That might be useful for diving after balls.</i>

00:09:53.100 --> 00:09:53.790
It went in...

00:09:54.280 --> 00:09:56.800
<i>Miyazaki has a pretty long reach.</i>

00:09:56.800 --> 00:10:00.750
<i>He's bad at figuring out where the ball goes, but on first, where catching is important...</i>

00:10:03.350 --> 00:10:05.480
Damn! I lost again...

00:10:05.480 --> 00:10:07.580
I'll win for sure next time!

00:10:08.010 --> 00:10:08.880
No way, no way!

00:10:08.880 --> 00:10:10.550
I won't lose if it's batting.

00:10:10.550 --> 00:10:13.600
<i>The long-legged Takahashi should be the center fielder.</i>

00:10:13.600 --> 00:10:17.140
<i>Since the three get along so well, if I put them together...</i>

00:10:17.140 --> 00:10:19.650
All right, keep them coming!

00:10:19.650 --> 00:10:20.340
Well...

00:10:20.340 --> 00:10:24.870
if there's an energetic guy in the middle of the field, it should help raise morale.

00:10:22.850 --> 00:10:24.290
{missing background tl}{AMS: tlc can't hear this}

00:10:24.870 --> 00:10:28.090
Is it really all right to decide like this?

00:10:30.450 --> 00:10:32.050
T-That was dangerous.

00:10:33.050 --> 00:10:33.480
Back! Back!

00:10:33.480 --> 00:10:34.110
Back! Back!

00:10:34.110 --> 00:10:34.990
All right!

00:10:34.990 --> 00:10:36.030
We'll leave it to you.

00:10:38.340 --> 00:10:40.000
But isn't it turning out really well?

00:10:43.210 --> 00:10:45.530
Uchiyama, what're you doing?

00:10:45.530 --> 00:10:49.040
Since we're practicing every day, the sewing work has piled up.

00:10:49.040 --> 00:10:51.640
I have to mend my siblings' clothing.

00:10:52.650 --> 00:10:54.140
You're quite the handyman.

00:10:54.910 --> 00:10:57.590
I'm sorry! I wasn't really ditching practice...

00:10:57.590 --> 00:10:58.940
Try standing in the batter's box.

00:11:05.230 --> 00:11:06.680
Not bad!

00:11:06.680 --> 00:11:09.500
All right, Uchiyama, you'll bat second.

00:11:09.500 --> 00:11:11.990
Starting today, bunt half of the pitches.

00:11:11.990 --> 00:11:13.190
A-All right.

00:11:13.190 --> 00:11:15.660
Hey, hey, we're even deciding on the batting order?

00:11:15.660 --> 00:11:17.330
I told you.

00:11:17.330 --> 00:11:22.910
We're going to work on each and every individual's talent, so that everyone can do the best they can.

00:11:22.910 --> 00:11:26.880
We must use this method if this team wants to win.

00:11:28.290 --> 00:11:29.900
Put your waist into it.

00:11:29.900 --> 00:11:32.330
It's your job to bring the runners home.

00:11:32.330 --> 00:11:35.590
At least hit an outfield fly.

00:11:35.590 --> 00:11:36.460
Yes, sir!

00:11:37.350 --> 00:11:39.540
<i>Tashiro, who's a candidate to be the fourth batter,</i>

00:11:39.540 --> 00:11:41.980
<i>is practicing specifically to hit the long ball.</i>

00:11:41.980 --> 00:11:44.560
<i>This is actually pretty easy to figure out.</i>

00:11:44.570 --> 00:11:49.570
This is a free fansub.

00:11:44.570 --> 00:11:49.570
Not for sale or rent.

00:11:51.000 --> 00:11:52.330
I'm home!

00:11:53.350 --> 00:11:54.680
Onii-chan, welcome home!

00:11:54.680 --> 00:11:55.800
Welcome home!

00:11:55.800 --> 00:11:58.580
Sorry, I'm late.

00:11:59.810 --> 00:12:01.550
Oh, welcome home!

00:12:01.550 --> 00:12:03.740
I'm sorry, Oba-san.

00:12:03.740 --> 00:12:05.250
You even took care of their dinner...

00:12:05.250 --> 00:12:09.930
Oh, it's fine! Just make sure you make it to Koshien, okay?

00:12:09.930 --> 00:12:13.630
So that your neighbors can be proud of that! 

00:12:23.010 --> 00:12:23.810
I'm home.

00:12:27.640 --> 00:12:30.000
Baseball practice till this late, huh?

00:12:30.000 --> 00:12:31.280
Really...

00:12:33.640 --> 00:12:38.740
Dad, I... want to test myself to see how far I can go!

00:12:39.590 --> 00:12:40.950
Do whatever you want.

00:12:40.950 --> 00:12:43.430
I won't accept baseball though.

00:12:46.350 --> 00:12:49.880
Ouch... My entire body is hurting...

00:12:51.280 --> 00:12:53.730
I should be a little more muscular now, right? 

00:13:02.060 --> 00:13:05.600
You're a true man, Home Run King, Ooki-kun!

00:13:05.600 --> 00:13:08.770
Weren't you doing special training for baseball?

00:13:08.770 --> 00:13:09.770
<i>I've been discovered!</i>

00:13:09.770 --> 00:13:15.150
"In the case that infielders interfere with the runners..."

00:13:15.150 --> 00:13:17.240
This is so hard!

00:13:18.620 --> 00:13:20.170
Studying the rules, huh?

00:13:20.170 --> 00:13:21.510
You're pretty passionate.

00:13:21.510 --> 00:13:23.670
She's the manager of the baseball team!

00:13:23.670 --> 00:13:25.710
She works hard till it's late every night!

00:13:26.200 --> 00:13:27.730
Isn't that great?

00:13:27.730 --> 00:13:30.380
Here, let me help. If it's baseball, your dad knows-

00:13:30.380 --> 00:13:31.770
Stop it!

00:13:34.600 --> 00:13:37.470
Up until now, you've treated me like I'm fragile.

00:13:37.470 --> 00:13:40.760
Are you that happy that I've found something to replace track?

00:13:45.260 --> 00:13:46.730
Miho...

00:14:07.560 --> 00:14:08.580
I got in!

00:14:08.870 --> 00:14:10.270
I waited for you!

00:14:11.410 --> 00:14:12.460
You did it!

00:14:19.260 --> 00:14:20.790
There it is! You passed!

00:14:20.790 --> 00:14:22.050
Well, that's for sure.

00:14:23.620 --> 00:14:25.020
{check timing and tl}{AMS: nothing other than incomprehensible female chattering here}

00:14:25.020 --> 00:14:26.490
I passed!

00:14:40.660 --> 00:14:41.430
You!

00:14:41.430 --> 00:14:42.350
Hey there!

00:14:42.350 --> 00:14:44.410
I had nothing to do, and it's spring break, so I stopped by!

00:14:44.970 --> 00:14:48.000
Did you leave the starting shortstop position open for me?

00:14:48.000 --> 00:14:48.810
Yo!

00:14:49.340 --> 00:14:50.880
Long time no see, Shimizu.

00:14:51.780 --> 00:14:53.590
Why is Coach Kashimoto here?

00:14:53.970 --> 00:14:57.260
I was looking forward to hitting hard liners at you.

00:15:05.350 --> 00:15:06.230
He's good...

00:15:06.230 --> 00:15:08.580
I guess experienced athletes are different.

00:15:08.580 --> 00:15:10.730
Guess he wasn't all talk.

00:15:10.730 --> 00:15:14.580
I see. What a reliable new member.

00:15:14.580 --> 00:15:17.070
We finally have nine members together.

00:15:17.070 --> 00:15:17.740
Yeah.

00:15:29.770 --> 00:15:32.460
Strike! Out! Game over!

00:15:34.920 --> 00:15:38.420
The Kanagawa representative, Kaido High, wins!

00:15:38.420 --> 00:15:44.390
With the amazing Mayamura-Sato battery, this year's Kaido High is said to be the strongest ever.

00:15:44.390 --> 00:15:46.070
Aiming towards winning both the spring and summer tournaments:

00:15:46.070 --> 00:15:49.850
With their overwhelming strength, they've won the spring tournament.

00:15:51.170 --> 00:15:55.060
Don't forget that in the summer I'm going to be standing up there.

00:15:58.530 --> 00:16:00.400
Sato-kun, you've got a letter.

00:16:00.400 --> 00:16:02.240
Oh, thank you.

00:16:02.240 --> 00:16:03.280
What is it?

00:16:03.280 --> 00:16:05.890
Is it another love letter from your girlfriend?

00:16:05.890 --> 00:16:07.580
I'm so jealous!

00:16:07.580 --> 00:16:09.450
Stop it. It's not like that.

00:16:10.090 --> 00:16:13.420
<i>Sato-senpai, congratulations on the win.</i>

00:16:14.100 --> 00:16:17.880
<i>My exams are done, and I finally feel relieved.</i>

00:16:17.880 --> 00:16:23.380
<i>After much hesitation, I ended up deciding to apply for Seishuu High, the school that I've admired for a long time.</i>

00:16:24.350 --> 00:16:25.590
Did she say "Seishuu"?

00:16:37.360 --> 00:16:40.960
<i>A new classroom, new friends...</i>

00:16:42.030 --> 00:16:45.800
<i>Right here, right now, my high school life is going to begin!</i>

00:16:45.800 --> 00:16:46.650
Excuse me...

00:16:46.650 --> 00:16:48.030
you're in the way.

00:16:48.530 --> 00:16:49.930
I-I'm sorry!

00:17:00.460 --> 00:17:04.710
Um, I'm Suzuki Ayane. It's nice to meet you.

00:17:04.710 --> 00:17:05.810
You too.

00:17:08.930 --> 00:17:10.160
Let's see...

00:17:10.160 --> 00:17:13.890
Shimizu Taiga-kun... What a wonderful name!

00:17:15.710 --> 00:17:21.330
Hey, could it be that you're trying to claim the guys first because there aren't many here?

00:17:21.330 --> 00:17:24.490
Sorry, but I'm not interested in younger girls.

00:17:24.490 --> 00:17:28.830
T-That's not it! I already have someone I like!

00:17:35.410 --> 00:17:39.000
<i>This guy... has such a bad attitude.</i>

00:17:43.850 --> 00:17:47.910
<i>High school baseball... It must be intense.</i>

00:17:47.910 --> 00:17:49.260
You're in the way.

00:17:50.570 --> 00:17:53.280
Um, Shimizu-kun, are you on the baseball team?

00:17:53.280 --> 00:17:55.770
I want to be the manager.

00:17:56.270 --> 00:17:57.940
You sure are unusual.

00:17:57.940 --> 00:18:01.770
If you want to be a manager, you should've gone to Kaido.

00:18:01.770 --> 00:18:06.140
W-Well, it's Kaido's policy that they don't hire student managers.

00:18:06.140 --> 00:18:07.900
Besides, if I take the regular classes,

00:18:07.900 --> 00:18:11.200
then I can only see Sato-senpai, who's in the sports program, during practice!

00:18:11.830 --> 00:18:15.290
Is the person you like that Sato-senpai?

00:18:16.750 --> 00:18:19.460
So he plays for Kaido, huh?

00:18:19.460 --> 00:18:23.630
It's unfortunate, but if he's from a junior high baseball team,
he's probably only on the second string.

00:18:23.630 --> 00:18:25.960
He's a regular on the first string, and he's the captain!

00:18:26.850 --> 00:18:29.640
By "Sato," you mean Kaido's clean-up hitter?

00:18:29.640 --> 00:18:32.850
Sato-senpai is truly incredible! 

00:18:32.850 --> 00:18:36.980
In junior high, he lost to that violent and rowdy guy, but...

00:18:38.340 --> 00:18:39.940
What'd you say, you bastard!?

00:18:39.940 --> 00:18:42.000
No matter how you look at it, it went in!

00:18:42.000 --> 00:18:43.930
The ball was halfway out!

00:18:43.930 --> 00:18:44.940
Hey, stop it!

00:18:46.670 --> 00:18:47.360
That person!

00:18:48.110 --> 00:18:48.820
Huh?

00:18:51.240 --> 00:18:53.650
Hey! Stop striking a pose every time!

00:18:53.650 --> 00:18:54.950
We're going again!

00:18:54.950 --> 00:18:57.420
All right! Come anytime!

00:18:58.460 --> 00:19:01.150
<i>That scary person is actually the captain...</i>

00:19:01.150 --> 00:19:02.880
<i>I wonder if I'll be all right.</i>

00:19:05.440 --> 00:19:08.220
Don't be so nervous, it's fine.

00:19:08.220 --> 00:19:10.470
If you don't understand something, just ask me!

00:19:10.470 --> 00:19:13.060
O-Okay! Please take care of me.

00:19:13.060 --> 00:19:15.780
All right! Let's move onto batting practice!

00:19:18.500 --> 00:19:19.680
What is that?

00:19:19.680 --> 00:19:21.290
It's a scorebook.

00:19:21.290 --> 00:19:24.510
I thought it might be good to record the batting scores.

00:19:24.510 --> 00:19:26.320
Then we can figure out the locations they're weak at.

00:19:27.760 --> 00:19:29.530
You know how to keep score?

00:19:29.530 --> 00:19:30.500
Teach me! Teach me!

00:19:30.500 --> 00:19:31.450
Teach me! Teach me!

00:19:32.060 --> 00:19:33.490
S-Sure...

00:19:34.110 --> 00:19:36.450
All right! Everyone gather around!

00:19:36.950 --> 00:19:40.160
These past few months, everyone really tried their hardest.

00:19:40.840 --> 00:19:43.330
We got some new members, and the team has come together.

00:19:43.860 --> 00:19:47.550
Tomorrow finally marks the beginning of Seishuu's official baseball team.

00:19:48.210 --> 00:19:54.510
Our work ends today, but I hope that from now on, you'll work together with Yamada-sensei and try your hardest!

00:19:55.140 --> 00:19:57.720
We're looking forward to your enthusiasm in the tournament.

00:19:57.720 --> 00:19:58.680
Yes, sir!

00:20:01.550 --> 00:20:03.220
Do your best, Goro.

00:20:03.220 --> 00:20:06.360
It's up to you... how far this team goes.

00:20:06.760 --> 00:20:08.830
Yeah, leave it to me.

00:20:08.830 --> 00:20:12.360
I'll definitely get these guys to Koshien.

00:20:15.250 --> 00:20:17.080
I see... 

00:20:17.080 --> 00:20:19.050
Well, when you have the chance...{(let me know if you need the names of the schools)}

00:20:24.570 --> 00:20:27.330
<i>As a baseball team, the first exhibition game...</i>

00:20:27.330 --> 00:20:30.210
<i>is the final step in becoming a real team.</i>

00:20:31.170 --> 00:20:33.560
<i>There's no point if the opponent's easy to beat.</i>

00:20:34.330 --> 00:20:39.180
<i>But... the stronger teams won't play a game with a no-name team like ours.</i>

00:20:46.030 --> 00:20:46.760
Yes?

00:20:47.460 --> 00:20:48.870
Yeah, I'll take it.

00:20:49.980 --> 00:20:54.430
The call's been transferred. This is Egashira, the assistant coach of the baseball team.

00:20:56.320 --> 00:20:57.970
An exhibition game?

00:20:58.480 --> 00:21:00.290
Where are you from?

00:21:00.700 --> 00:21:03.010
How untimely... Our schedule's already fixed for the next two months. 

00:21:06.040 --> 00:21:07.700
Seishuu High School?

00:21:12.180 --> 00:21:15.130
We have our opponent for our first exhibition game.

00:21:15.650 --> 00:21:19.100
This Sunday at 1pm. The place is Atsugi.

00:21:19.480 --> 00:21:20.810
<i>Atsugi?</i>

00:21:20.810 --> 00:21:24.390
Our opponent is Kaido High School's second string.

00:21:25.250 --> 00:21:26.100
What!?

00:21:26.100 --> 00:21:28.560
K-Kaido's second string?

00:21:28.950 --> 00:21:32.680
Even if they're the second string,
they're the next to make Kaido's main team.

00:21:32.680 --> 00:21:34.700
They are strong enough for you guys.

00:21:35.450 --> 00:21:38.140
We're too weak for them!

00:21:38.970 --> 00:21:41.100
Are we going to lose so suddenly?

00:21:41.100 --> 00:21:42.530
I won't let them.

00:21:44.670 --> 00:21:47.370
I won't let them beat us badly.

00:21:52.300 --> 00:21:54.510
Seishuu and our second string?

00:21:54.510 --> 00:21:55.950
Y-Yes.

00:21:55.950 --> 00:21:59.620
Just a few moments ago, there was a phone call from Egashira-san,

00:21:59.620 --> 00:22:03.470
saying that he would take care of all the strategies for that day.

00:22:03.470 --> 00:22:05.380
What's going on?

00:22:05.380 --> 00:22:11.520
Even if Shigeno-kun is there, there's no merit in having a game with a no-name school like Seishuu.

00:22:11.520 --> 00:22:14.230
Seems like something's fishy.

00:22:14.690 --> 00:22:17.730
He even tried to stop Shigeno-kun from transferring...

00:22:18.280 --> 00:22:20.910
To take us off the bench...

00:22:20.910 --> 00:22:23.760
for this game, he must have something planned...

00:22:34.510 --> 00:22:36.850
That's Kaido's second string, huh?

00:22:36.850 --> 00:22:39.060
I feel like I can see their auras.

00:22:39.740 --> 00:22:44.240
W-What? If Shigeno's here, we'll do something somehow.

00:22:44.240 --> 00:22:45.520
Right?

00:22:46.190 --> 00:22:47.980
Yo! It's been a while!

00:22:48.600 --> 00:22:50.820
Thanks for accepting a game with us.

00:22:51.790 --> 00:22:53.690
It wasn't us.

00:22:53.690 --> 00:22:56.320
Be careful, Shigeno-kun.

00:22:56.320 --> 00:23:00.160
The reason for this game is probably because Egashira is targeting you.

00:24:40.910 --> 00:24:42.980
If we can't defeat Kaido's second string,

00:24:42.980 --> 00:24:45.010
there's no way we'll be able to defeat Toshiya and the rest of the main team!

00:24:45.770 --> 00:24:48.580
I don't know what Egashira is planning,

00:24:48.580 --> 00:24:51.810
but we'll have you guys become our practice targets.

00:24:52.510 --> 00:24:53.980
Next time, on Major:

00:24:53.980 --> 00:24:55.060
Egashira's Plot.

00:24:55.740 --> 00:24:58.120
Run to the stage of your dreams!
